.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt PMSET 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm pmset
.Nd manipulate power management settings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl g Op Cm live | custom | cap | batt | ps | assertions | sched | therm | uuid | log
.Nm
.Op Fl a | c | b | u
.Ar setting value ...
.Nm
.Cm sleepnow | displaysleepnow | restoredefaults | touch | noidle
.Nm
.Cm disablesleep Cm 0 | 1
.Nm
.Cm schedule Op Cm cancel
.Ar type Qq Ar MM/dd/yy HH:mm:ss
.Op Ar owner
.Nm
.Cm repeat Cm cancel | Ar type weekdays HH:mm:ss
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and changes the power management settings, through IOKit's power
functions and
.Xr powerd 8 ,
which applies them.
Changes need root.
.Ss Reading
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl g , Fl g Cm live
The settings in use, for the power source the machine draws from.
On a machine that cannot sleep,
.Cm sleep
says so.
.It Fl g Cm custom
The settings of each power source the machine has.
.It Fl g Cm cap
The settings this machine supports.
.It Fl g Cm batt , Fl g Cm ps
The power source in use and the batteries or UPSes known.
.It Fl g Cm assertions
The assertions held: their status by type and each process's, with how
long it has held them.
.It Fl g Cm sched
Scheduled and repeating power events.
.It Fl g Cm therm , Cm uuid , Cm log
Thermal state, the sleep/wake UUID, the log (none yet on this system).
.El
.Ss Settings
.Fl a
(the default),
.Fl c ,
.Fl b
and
.Fl u
change the settings of all power sources, AC power, battery or UPS:
.Cm displaysleep , disksleep
and
.Cm sleep
(minutes, 0 or
.Cm never
to turn them off),
.Cm womp , ring , autorestart , lidwake , acwake , lessbright , halfdim ,
.Cm ttyskeepawake , hibernatemode , hibernatefile , standby ,
.Cm standbydelay , autopoweroff , autopoweroffdelay , powernap ,
.Cm tcpkeepalive , networkoversleep , proximitywake , gpuswitch , dps .
.Ss Actions
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm sleepnow
Sleep now; refused where the machine cannot sleep.
.It Cm displaysleepnow
Put the display to sleep now.
.It Cm restoredefaults
Back to the default settings.
.It Cm touch
Apply the settings again.
.It Cm noidle
Keep the system from idle sleep until interrupted.
.It Cm disablesleep Cm 1 | 0
Disable or allow system sleep; a machine that cannot sleep keeps it
disabled.
.It Cm schedule
Schedule (or cancel) a
.Cm sleep , wake , poweron , shutdown , wakeorpoweron
or
.Cm restart
at a date and time.
.It Cm repeat
A weekly event on the days given (a subset of
.Li MTWRFSU )
at a time of day, or
.Cm cancel
them.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr caffeinate 8 ,
.Xr powerd 8 ,
.Xr systemsetup 8
